Yes... umm. I agree with that, but I'm not sure how it relates to what
you quoted. Perhaps I didn't express myself clearly. Take this
example: if you throw a food ration into the lava, it will say that
the food ration burns (although if you dig it up, it will still be
ok). However if you wish for a fireproof food ration and then throw
that into the lava, it will not burn - but "fireproof" doesn't appear
in its description. Also, if you are holding a fireproof food ration,
and you pick up a non-fireproof ration which has the same BUC status,
they will merge and you will now have two fireproof rations.

It's not really a big deal, it's just a bit weird.


Regarding K-Mod; I've just downloaded some Git software, and I'm going
to try to transfer my svn history to git and then clone the git stuff
on sourceforge. So soon there will be a public repository; probably
sometime today, but maybe later. As for the mod itself, I've made a
stack more changes. Here's a partial list for anyone who's interested.

+ mixing potions no longer clears BUC knowledge
+ clearing with unicorn horn no longer clears BUC knowledge (but still
sets to uncursed for water)
+ +1 to-hit for all shortswords
+ covetous monsters will not try to harrass you if they are peaceful
+ beam hit probabilities now depends on dex rather than ac. Compared
to the old system, wands will miss more in the early game and hit more
in the late game.
+ 'enchant weapon' can now be used to fooproof bags (and some other
stuff) as well as weapons
+ added K-Mod version info to patchlevel.h
+ implemented some rudimentary version conversion routines for save /
bone files. It is now possible to add new items without breaking
bones / save compatibility.
+ now moves broken files to troubledir rather than deleting them.
+ New item: helm of anti-magic / horned helmet. It gives magic
resistance, but also has some negative side effects.
+ adjusted the graphics for the silver short sword, and added new
graphics for the horned helmet.

The BUC knowledge stuff was to make it consistent with diluting
potions in fountains and such.

The beam hit probability (zap_hit in the code) is a pretty significant
change. I decided that it was a bit silly that early in the game,
beams pretty much always hit and a quite dangerous; and then later in
the game when you have more hp, and resistance and everything, beams
almost always miss! Furthermore, I don't like that AC was protecting
against pretty much everything. I've been trying to make AC only help
against physical attacks, and not so much against magical attacks
(such as the beam from a wand of fire).

The helm of anti-magic will sometimes absorb spells that you are
trying to cast; and it will sometimes stun you if you resist a spell
while wearing it. It's not really a viable option for spell casters,
but I can imagine using it as a barbarian for example - and maybe then
wearing orange dragon scale mail armour. Also, the existence of this
helm makes it less trivial to identify a helm of brilliance. To me,
the best part is that I was able to add this item without breaking my
bones files or save files. (actually there is a minor problem with the
save file conversion: when an old save is converted, the new item may
end up being made from the material of one of the items it gets
shuffled with, instead of using its own material).

I've also made some other minor changes, such as slightly decreasing
the probability that a ring will explode when it is charged. But
that's about all.


